      "prompt": "You translate ordinary questions into exactly one read-only DuckDB SELECT or WITH query.\n\nReturn SQL only. Never write files, install software, calculate values yourself, or invent columns.\n\nUse only the supplied schema. Preserve relevant scope from earlier turns unless the newest question changes it.\n\nA requested rate must use its stated numerator and denominator. Percentage-point change means later percentage minus earlier percentage, not relative growth.\n\nWhen the user explicitly asks for percent or percentage, multiply numerator divided by denominator by 100.\n\nWhen the user asks to compare years or groups without asking for a change, keep those year/group columns and requested measures in the output.\n\nWhen several known category values are named, filter them separately with IN rather than concatenating them.\n\nUse NULLIF for denominators. Missing values remain missing and are not zero.\n\nSCHEMA:\nCREATE TABLE \"attendance_2023\" (\n  \"Centre\" VARCHAR,\n  \"Month\" VARCHAR,\n  \"Enrolled Kids\" BIGINT,\n  \"Avg Daily Present\" BIGINT\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE \"attendance_2024\" (\n  \"centre_name\" VARCHAR,\n  \"month\" VARCHAR,\n  \"enrolment\" BIGINT,\n  \"average_attendance\" BIGINT\n);\n\nKNOWN CATEGORICAL VALUES (local or trusted 27B tier only):\n{\"attendance_2023\": {\"Centre\": [\"Chembur Balwadi\", \"Dharavi Balwadi\", \"Govandi Balwadi\", \"Kurla Balwadi\", \"Mankhurd Balwadi\", \"Sion Balwadi\", \"Wadala Balwadi\", \"Worli Balwadi\"], \"Month\": [\"April\", \"August\", \"December\", \"February\", \"January\", \"July\", \"June\", \"March\", \"May\", \"November\", \"October\", \"September\"]}, \"attendance_2024\": {\"centre_name\": [\"Chembur Balwadi\", \"Dharavi Balwadi\", \"Govandi Balwadi\", \"Kurla Balwadi\", \"Mankhurd Balwadi\", \"Sion Balwadi\", \"Wadala Balwadi\", \"Worli Balwadi\"], \"month\": [\"April\", \"August\", \"December\", \"February\", \"January\", \"July\", \"June\", \"March\", \"May\", \"November\", \"October\", \"September\"]}}\n\nCURRENT QUESTION:\nrank centres by how much their turnout percentage dropped between the two years, worst first",
      "response": "```sql\nWITH attendance_2023_percentage AS (\n  SELECT\n    \"Centre\",\n    \"Month\",\n    (\"Avg Daily Present\" * 100.0 / NULLIF(\"Enrolled Kids\", 0)) AS \"Turnout Percentage 2023\"\n  FROM\n    \"attendance_2023\"\n),\nattendance_2024_percentage AS (\n  SELECT\n    \"centre_name\" AS \"Centre\",\n    \"month\" AS \"Month\",\n    (\"average_attendance\" * 100.0 / NULLIF(\"enrolment\", 0)) AS \"Turnout Percentage 2024\"\n  FROM\n    \"attendance_2024\"\n),\ncombined_turnout AS (\n  SELECT\n    a3.\"Centre\",\n    a3.\"Month\",\n    a3.\"Turnout Percentage 2023\",\n    a4.\"Turnout Percentage 2024\",\n    (a4.\"Turnout Percentage 2024\" - a3.\"Turnout Percentage 2023\") AS \"Percentage Change\"\n  FROM\n    attendance_2023_percentage a3\n  JOIN\n    attendance_2024_percentage a4\n  ON\n    a3.\"Centre\" = a4.\"Centre\" AND a3.\"Month\" = a4.\"Month\"\n)\nSELECT\n  \"Centre\",\n  \"Month\",\n  \"Percentage Change\" AS \"Turnout Percentage Drop\"\nFROM\n  combined_turnout\nORDER BY\n  \"Percentage Change\" ASC;\n```",
